hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1739","**\nNarrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb: narrated to us my uncle (Ibn Wahb), who informed me from Makhramah, from his father, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa al-Ash'ari (RA), who said:\n'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (RA) said to me, \Did you hear your father narrating from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding the time of acceptance of supplication on Friday?\""\nI said"," \""Yes"," I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say:\n'It is between the time when the imam sits on the pulpit until the prayer is completed.'\""\n\nNarrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman: narrated to us my uncle"," who informed me from Maymun ibn Yahya — and he is the son of the brother of Makhramah — from Makhramah"," from his father"," with this chain of narration similarly."""
